WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.610
Attention Is All You Need — the paper that introduced the
Transformer.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:14.076
From Google Brain, Google Research and the University of
Toronto, published at NeurIPS 2017.

00:00:15.426 --> 00:00:26.274
In 2017 the best sequence models were recurrent. To compute
the hidden state at position t, you first need the state at t

00:00:26.724 --> 00:00:36.084
That dependency chain is the problem. Within a training
example, nothing can be parallelised — you march through the

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:45.462
And information from the first token has to survive n hops to
reach the last one, which is why long-range dependencies were

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:56.424
Self-attention breaks both at once. Every position is computed
simultaneously, and any position can reach any other in a

00:00:56.874 --> 00:01:05.970
The paper's claim in the title is literal: remove recurrence
and convolution entirely, and attention alone is enough.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.824
Here is the operation, not the box.

00:01:11.274 --> 00:01:21.162
Every position emits three vectors: a query for what it is
looking for, a key for what it offers, and a value for what it

00:01:21.612 --> 00:01:30.228
Take the query from the word 'it'. Dot it against every key in
the sentence. That gives a similarity score per position.

00:01:30.678 --> 00:01:39.246
Softmax turns those scores into weights that sum to one. The
output for 'it' is the weighted sum of all the values.

00:01:39.696 --> 00:01:46.320
The word 'animal' scores highest, so most of the output comes
from it — which is how 'it' gets resolved.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:56.682
The crucial part: these weights are computed, not learned. The
same weights matrix does not exist. It is recomputed for every

00:01:58.032 --> 00:02:00.984
Written as a computation, it is short.

00:02:01.434 --> 00:02:15.090
Multiply queries by keys transposed to get all the scores at
once. Divide by the square root of the key dimension.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:26.532
That is the entire attention function, and every operation in
it is a matrix multiply or an elementwise map — which is

00:02:26.982 --> 00:02:33.534
Doing it for all queries at once is what buys the parallelism
the previous slide promised.

00:02:34.884 --> 00:02:39.132
The scaling factor looks like an arbitrary detail and is not.

00:02:39.582 --> 00:02:50.358
If the query and key components are independent with unit
variance, their dot product has variance d-k. With d-k of 64,

00:02:50.808 --> 00:03:02.592
Large logits push softmax into its saturated region — one
weight goes to nearly one, the rest to nearly zero, and the

00:03:03.042 --> 00:03:12.570
Dividing by the square root of d-k puts the variance back at
one, which keeps the distribution informative and the

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:21.684
The paper notes this is why the dot-product form works at all
at scale; without it, additive attention outperforms it.

00:03:23.034 --> 00:03:28.962
A single attention is a single weighted average, and averaging
destroys information.

00:03:29.412 --> 00:03:39.204
If one head has to encode subject agreement and coreference
and positional adjacency all at once, it has to compromise

00:03:39.654 --> 00:03:49.182
Multi-head attention runs h attentions in parallel, each on
its own learned projection of the queries, keys and values.

00:03:49.632 --> 00:03:57.840
One head can track what 'it' refers to while another tracks
the verb it attaches to and a third tracks adjacent words.

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:09.474
The paper's appendix shows exactly this: individual heads
learn behaviours that look like syntactic and semantic

00:04:10.824 --> 00:04:13.944
The implementation keeps the cost flat.

00:04:14.394 --> 00:04:22.866
With a model dimension of 512 and eight heads, each head works
in 64 dimensions rather than 512.

00:04:23.316 --> 00:04:30.948
So the eight heads together cost about the same as one full-
width attention. You get the diversity for free.

00:04:31.398 --> 00:04:40.566
The outputs are concatenated and passed through one more
learned projection, W-O, which lets the model mix what the

00:04:41.916 --> 00:04:54.204
Attention has a problem recurrence did not: it is permutation
